    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"The displayed sources show that policy debate is mainly driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_4068201611ccbb4d\",\"quote\":\"These changes to the Health and Safety at Work etc. Act 1974 have their origin in the report of Professor Löfstedt entitled Reclaiming Health and Safety for All, in which he recommended that those self-employed people whose activities posed no potential risk of harm to others should be exempt from the general duties under that Act. Their main duty was to carry out an assessment of…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_e0e65d592ca003db\",\"quote\":\"On the subject of China, the Prime Minister is indeed talking to the Chinese on the subject of steel and the necessary restructuring. Of course, it is not only a matter for bilateral discussion, because anti-dumping is a matter for the EU: 28 countries together can do more.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"absence of a warrant demonstrating that institutional procedures and formal paperwork *mainly* drive policy debate.\",\"mechanism\":\"Misrepresentation of evidence scope.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim oversimplifies the complex drivers of policy debate, ignoring broader economic, social, and political factors.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The cited sources discuss the influence of reports, international agreements, and specific policy initiatives, but do not establish that institutional procedures and paperwork are the *main* drivers.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The evidence demonstrates that policy debate is influenced by a range of factors beyond institutional procedures and paperwork, undermining the claim's central assertion. The sources highlight reports, international agreements, and specific policy initiatives, indicating a more complex landscape than the claim suggests.\"}",
